        <body>
            <div xml:id="d64">

                <pb facs="0174" n="72" sameAs="frus:frus1908/pg72"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 2413/208–209.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Chinese Minister.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1908-12-31"><hi rendition="#italic">December 31,
                        1908</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to transmit herewith a
                    copy of an Executive order, dated December 28, 1908, providing, under the joint
                    resolution or congress of May 25, 1908, for the remission of a portion of the
                    indemnity against the losses and expenses incurred by reason of the so-called
                    Boxer disturbances in Peking during the year 1900.</p>
                <p>It affords me great pleasure to inform you that such remission will begin upon
                    the 1st day of January, 1909.</p>
                <p>Accept, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Elihu Root.</hi></signed></closer>






